/a></li>\n<li id=\"menu-item-231\" class=\"menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-231\"><a href=\"https://venomcoding.org/download-codes/\">Download codes</a></li>\n<li id=\"menu-item-31\" class=\"menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-31\"><a href=\"https://venomcoding.org/terms-and-conditions/\">Terms and Conditions</a></li>\n<li id=\"menu-item-190\" class=\"menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-190\"><a href=\"https://venomcoding.org/history/\">History</a></li>\n<li id=\"menu-item-30\" class=\"menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-30\"><a href=\"https://venomcoding.org/contact-us/\">Contact Us</a></li>\n</ul></div>\n\t</nav><!-- #site-navigation -->\n\n\t\n</div>\n\n\t\t\t\n<nav class=\"social-menu\">\n\n\t\n</nav><!-- .social-menu -->\n\n\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t\n<div class=\"hero\">\n\n\t\n\t<div class=\"hero-inner\">\n\n\t\t\n<div class=\"page-title-container\">\n\n\t<header class=\"page-header\">\n\n\t\t<h1 class=\"page-title\">VeNom Codes</h1>\n\t</header><!-- .entry-header -->\n\n</div><!-- .page-title-container -->\n\n\t</div>\n\n</div>\n\n\t</header><!-- #masthead -->\n\n\t<div id=\"page\" class=\"hfeed site\">\n\n\t\t<div id=\"content\" class=\"site-content\">\n\n<div id=\"primary\" class=\"content-area\">\n\n\t<main id=\"main\" class=\"site-main\" role=\"main\">\n\n\t\t\n<article id=\"post-21\" class=\"post-21 page type-page status-publish hentry\">\n\n\t\n\t\n<div class=\"page-content\">\n\n\t\n<p>The VeNom Codes are stored in a central Database Dictionary that is maintained by the Royal Veterinary College. Within the dictionary, each code (Term name) is allocated a unique numeric identifier (Database Dictionary Id) and codes are grouped according to the type of term under a Label, e.g. Diagnosis, Presenting complaint. </p>\n\n\n\n<p>Below is a screenshot of a selection of the codes as they appear in Excel.</p>\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
